"Let $t$ be the number of hours Jane started growing Sphere. Then, she started growing Rod for $t-5$ hours.\n\nThe population of Rod doubles every hour, so the population of Rod after $t-5$ hours is $2\\cdot2^{(t-5)}$.\n\nThe population of Sphere quadruples every hour, so the population of Sphere after $t$ hours is $8\\cdot4^{t}$.\n\nSince the populations are equal, we have:\n\n$$2\\cdot2^{(t-5)} = 8\\cdot4^{t}$$\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n$$2^{(t-5)} = 4^{t}$$\n\nSince $4 = 2^2$, we have:\n\n$$2^{(t-5)} = 2^{2t}$$\n\nSince the bases are the same, we can equate the exponents:\n\n$$t-5 = 2t$$\n\nSolving for $t$, we get:\n\n$$t = 5$$\n\nTherefore, Jane started growing Sphere $\\boxed{5}$ hours ago."
