"To determine the number of ways to select 4 members out of 8, we use the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of items, and \\( k \\) is the number of items to choose.\n\nHere, \\( n = 8 \\) and \\( k = 4 \\).\n\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{4} = \\frac{8!}{4!(8-4)!} = \\frac{8!}{4! \\cdot 4!}\n=\\frac{8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 5}{4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{3360}{24} = 70\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to select 4 members out of 8 is \\(\\boxed{70}\\)."
