"The expected value of a coin flip is the weighted average of the outcomes. The outcomes are winning 2 dollars for heads and losing 1 dollar for tails. The probabilities are $\\frac{3}{4}\\) for heads and \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) for tails.\n\nThe expected value \\(E\\) is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\nE = \\left( \\frac{3}{4} \\times 2 \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{4} \\times (-1) \\right)\n\\]\n\n\\[\nE = \\frac{6}{4} - \\frac{1}{4}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nE = \\frac{5}{4}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nE = 1.25\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expected value of a coin flip is \\(\\boxed{1.25}\\)."
